Maintainer: TheMojoMan <themojoman@gmx.net>
Depends: libgbm1 (>= 27.0.0~devel.git234733.g8df830aa844-1erhai1), mesa-libgallium (>= 27.0.0~devel.git234733.g8df830aa844-1erhai1), libgl1-mesa-dri (>= 27.0.0~devel.git234733.g8df830aa844-1erhai1), libglx-mesa0 (>= 27.0.0~devel.git234733.g8df830aa844-1erhai1), libegl-mesa0 (>= 27.0.0~devel.git234733.g8df830aa844-1erhai1), mesa-vulkan-drivers (>= 27.0.0~devel.git234733.g8df830aa844-1erhai1)
Installed-Size: 0
Description: erhai Mesa development build (meta package)
 One name that pulls in the erhai Mesa /usr replacement -- the six
 Ubuntu-named packages libgbm1, mesa-libgallium, libgl1-mesa-dri,
 libglx-mesa0, libegl-mesa0 and mesa-vulkan-drivers rebuilt from mesa git
 for the Adreno 830 in the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai).
 .
 The six packages keep Ubuntu's names on purpose: libglx0/libegl1 hard-depend
 on them and their runtime siblings are pinned with exact "=" versions, so a
 differently named package could never take over those dependencies.  This
 meta package gives that set a single, release-independent name: it lives in
 the main suite and its version floor refuses the install on a release where
 the erhai Mesa build does not exist yet, instead of silently falling back to
 stock Ubuntu Mesa (which cannot drive the Adreno 830).
